docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:266:### `audit_log`
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:268:UC-005 extended the shared audit table with authenticated `user_id`, role, IP address, and structured `details`. The actor foreign key supports identity traceability, while nullable actor/entity identifiers permit events such as unknown-email login failures. Audit events remain append-oriented through the service/API surface.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:294:Provides authenticated actor ID, role, active/disabled state, password hash, and employee-to-staff link. It is referenced by generation, cancellation, audit records, and the canonical calculation-run actor FK.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:303:| `user_account` | `audit_log` | 1:M, optional on child | Attributes audit activity |
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:338:| Cancelled-file restriction | Service | CSV download rejects cancelled batches; cancelled batches cannot be synchronized |
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:339:| Audit actor integrity | Database + service | Nullable `user_id` FK identifies known actors; service appends context and exposes no audit mutation API |
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:340:| Sensitive bank audit detail | Service/test | Bank-update audit stores field names only; test confirms raw account number is absent |
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:386:`payment_batch_item` captures the exact employee reference/name, bank destination, gross/incentive/CPF/SDL/other deduction/net values, and payment reference used for a Payment Batch. CSV/GIRO output and mock HRMS payloads read these rows, so later changes to `staff` or `payroll_lines` do not rewrite historical payment output.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:390:The benefits are historical accuracy, reproducible payment evidence, stable downstream output, and auditability. “Immutable” here describes the implemented write-once service/API pattern; it is not a claim that database triggers reject direct SQL updates.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:395:- `payment_batch.generated_by`, `cancelled_by`, and `audit_log.user_id` link financial/security activity to authenticated identities.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:398:- `BANK_DETAILS_UPDATED` audit details contain only the updated field names, not the submitted account number; canonical tests verify this.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:400:- `audit_log.details` is flexible JSONB, so services must continue to avoid inserting secrets. Current UC-005 services use scoped metadata.
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:409:| Completed Payment Batch | `payment_batch.status = completed`, HRMS status completed, HRMS reference present | One immutable item, one payslip, and `HRMS_SYNC_SUCCESS` audit event for paid period `...0005` |
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:410:| HRMS failure / retry | `payment_batch.status = hrms_sync_failed`, HRMS status failed, error message retained | One item, no seeded payslip, and `HRMS_SYNC_FAILURE` audit event for period `...0006` |
docs\kokenqi\database-schema.md:411:| Cancelled Payment Batch | `payment_batch.status = cancelled`, HRMS status `not_started`, cancellation actor/time/reason present | One retained item and `PAYMENT_BATCH_CANCELLED` audit event for period `...0007` |
